# A lens on three files: `save`, `saveOutage` and `keepSummary` put a Reading, an Outage and a Summary into their
# files, and `history`, `kept` and `keptSummary` get each back as the type it was put as, or inside a Harvest. `summary`
# is the lens at work: the kept summary, else (`??`) one made from the day's readings and put. `keptSummary` runs
# whenever `summary` does, and `??` chooses only whether the right side runs, as the `None` arm of Rust's `match` does;
# `keptSummary` builds its Summary only when a line is found (`line && ..`, a choice as `||` is). The route of the
# exported class is its constructor and its public methods, each called by its caller, run on the ReadingStore the
# constructor built. A library's operation whose result the body names (`find`, `map`) is a step; what it touches stays
# its caller's. Each file is read, used and written by the route: it stands on both sides.
#
# #new: new-A a parameter at the own arrow by its type, new-B an own arrow taking every class its steps build, new-C an
# unnamed call in a chain a step, new-E a value in one arm made by the choice, new-F a class's read-and-written place
# between, new-G an own arrow dropping a value it uses and hands on, new-I `??`'s left side an arm, new-J `&&` no choice
#.

